 "paragraphs": [
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p001.s01",
     "source": "It is said that when Lion and Gurikhoisip (the Only man), together with Baboon, Buffalo, and other friends, were playing one day at a certain game, there was a thunderstorm and rain at Aroxaams."
    },
    {
     "id": "p001.s02",
     "source": "Lion and Gurikhoisip began to quarrel."
    },
    {
     "id": "p001.s03",
     "source": "\"I shall run to the rain-field,\" said Lion."
    },
    {
     "id": "p001.s04",
     "source": "Gurikhoisip said also, \"I shall run to the rain-field.\""
    },
    {
     "id": "p001.s05",
     "source": "As neither would concede this to the other, they separated (angrily)."
    },
    {
     "id": "p001.s06",
     "source": "After they had parted, Lion went to tell his Mother those things which they had both said."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p001"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p002.s01",
     "source": "His Mother said to him, \"My son! that Man whose head is in a line with his shoulders and breast, who has pinching weapons, who keeps white dogs, who goes about wearing the tuft of a tiger's tail, beware of him!\""
    },
    {
     "id": "p002.s02",
     "source": "Lion, however, said, \"Why need I be on my guard against those whom I know?\""
    },
    {
     "id": "p002.s03",
     "source": "Lioness answered, \"My Son, take care of him who has pinching weapons!\""
    },
    {
     "id": "p002.s04",
     "source": "But Lion would not follow his Mother's advice, and the same morning, when it was still pitch dark, he went to Aroxaams, and laid himself in ambush."
    },
    {
     "id": "p002.s05",
     "source": "Gurikhoisip went also that morning to the same place."
    },
    {
     "id": "p002.s06",
     "source": "When he had arrived he let his dogs drink, and then bathe."
    },
    {
     "id": "p002.s07",
     "source": "After they had finished they wallowed."
    },
    {
     "id": "p002.s08",
     "source": "Then also Man drank; and, when he had done drinking, Lion came out of the bush."
    },
    {
     "id": "p002.s09",
     "source": "Dogs surrounded him as his Mother had foretold, and he was speared by Gurikhoisip."
    },
    {
     "id": "p002.s10",
     "source": "Just as he became aware that he was speared, the Dogs drew him down again."
    },
    {
     "id": "p002.s11",
     "source": "In this manner he grew faint."
    },
    {
     "id": "p002.s12",
     "source": "While he was in this state, Gurikhoisip said to the Dogs, \"Let him alone now, that he may go and be taught by his Mother.\""
    },
    {
     "id": "p002.s13",
     "source": "So the Dogs let him go."
    },
    {
     "id": "p002.s14",
     "source": "They left him, and went home as he lay there."
    },
    {
     "id": "p002.s15",
     "source": "The same night he walked towards home, but whilst he was on the way his strength failed him, and he lamented:"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p002"
  },
